  "findings": [
    "The app currently depends on Radio Browser KR entries, hides broken entries, requires HTTPS, caps the list at 60, and deduplicates by directory UUID rather than broadcast identity.",
    "KBS national channels 21-26 and regional 10_21 return fresh playable URLs from channel_item[].service_url. Select media_type radio or local, not bora.",
    "MBC must use sminiplay.imbc.com, not miniplay.imbc.com; the latter returned an empty response in this investigation.",
    "MBC and SBS endpoints return fresh plain-text streaming URLs. Expiring CDN query strings should be resolved at playback time and should not be persisted as channel identity.",
    "Existing directory URLs for KBS Classic FM, KBS Cool FM, KBS_kor and SBS Power FM returned HTTP 403; MBC FM returned HTTP 400. Fresh official endpoint URLs returned valid HLS.",
    "TBN Gyeongin, FEBC Seoul and BBS Seoul have responding HTTPS candidates, despite being absent from the current directory-derived app list.",
    "KBS 3Radio, MBC standard FM, SBS Power FM, TBN Gyeongin, FEBC Seoul, BBS Seoul and EBS FM yielded HLS child media data with HTTP 200; samples were capped at 2048 bytes and not saved as audio.",
    "The public repository README includes stale names/URLs (including swapped SBS labels and duplicate CBS URLs). Use current source and official player endpoints, not blind README copying.",
    "226 menu entries yield 193 distinct audio selectors after duplicate selectors and the visual-radio entry are removed. This is not a verified playable-channel count or a claim of exhaustive national coverage."
  ]
